RUN: `bash interface/verify/panel-lint.sh` (needs node >= 22, curl, jq, python3, unshare, ip, ss, Chrome at /usr/bin/google-chrome or $CHROME). Env: PANEL_LINT_BUNDLE=<dir> (real bundle), PANEL_LINT_KNOWN_GAPS=1, PANEL_LINT_SKIP_BUILD=1, PANEL_LINT_DWELL=10, PANEL_LINT_KEEP=1. shellcheck clean. 3 consecutive runs gave identical counts (no flake seen). The node under test is a REAL `111 daemon` supervising the stub meshmud (bin/meshmud wrapper), a fake presence reader (venvs/presence -> python3) and a devices.json Meshtastic binding (tcp://127.0.0.1:14403, a fake board), so `meshtastic` goes LIVE by itself and the panel is enabled through the real path. Namespace: lo + dummy0 192.168.77.5 and .9, no default route (asserted).

SIBLING INTERACTION: (1) the working tree is dirty with other sessions' edits (git status: many modified files incl. ui/src/views/services/panel*.tsx; V1 files smoke.sh, stub-llama.py, tcp-lan-relay.py, tapes/*) — my runs built whatever was on disk at ~00:00–00:30 on 2026-10-15; guard.rs itself is unmodified (gap #1 is at HEAD). (2) V1's smoke is already running MY interface/verify/stub-meshmud.py (`--role board --listen 127.0.0.1:4403`, `--role meshmud start-daemon …`), so I stopped changing it; its CLI/roles are now a shared contract. (3) Default mode runs `pnpm build` into ui/dist, like smoke.sh: do not run it concurrently with smoke.sh (a vite rebuild mid-run can flake either one).

WHAT IS ASSERTED (lan = paired LAN visitor over http://192.168.77.5, localhost = http://localhost -> 308 -> 127.0.0.1; every Network.requestWillBeSent over CDP on page, iframe, worker and popup targets, raw headers via *ExtraInfo): panel document loaded + 29 panel-made requests (non-vacuous); every panel-made request goes to its own origin; whole recording touches only the node host; no WebSocket (webSocketCreated on any target); no popup; no panel->dashboard request; no Access-Control-* on any of 36 panel responses (refusals included); every panel response has no X-Frame-Options, frame-ancestors = http://<host>:11180 http://<host>:80 ('none' only on guard refusals), nosniff, no-referrer; ticket in exactly one request URL (the 303 swap), none in Referer/Location/final URLs; swap Set-Cookie = `p111_meshtastic=<hex>; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict; Path=/` (no Domain/Max-Age/Secure) and the jar entry httpOnly/Strict/host-only/session; document.cookie in the frame is empty; exactly one iframe, on the panel origin, sandbox = the 6-token default set (no top-navigation), allow = `serial; bluetooth` = manifest; GET /api/v1/panels == the toml; dashboard CSP frame-src = exactly the panel origin, frame-ancestors 'none' + XFO DENY; shim round trip from the panel (PUT toradio 200, 11 GET fromradio?all=true 200 with frames, 3 nodes, 0 errors); Reload re-mints (new POST, new ticket, 303); spent ticket in a fresh browser = 403 panel_ticket_expired, no cookie; localhost 308 then the panel frames and runs. Static bundle lint (offline, on the served dir): all src/href relative, no on*= handler, no javascript:, inline-script count, third-party hostnames by grep (info). Canary: a hostile bundle (font CDN, script CDN, pixel, telemetry, WebSocket, dashboard call, declared optional host, onclick) is flagged by exactly the leak rules and the optional host is a note; files restored after.

